IMPORT prelude

-- Privacy Act 1988 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- whom the Act reaches (ss 6C, 6D, 6DA, 6EA: the small business operator
-- exemption and the $3,000,000 turnover test), direct marketing (Australian Privacy Principle 7 in Schedule 1), what a credit
-- reporting body may hold and for how long (Part IIIA: ss 6N, 6Q, 20C, 20V, 20W, 20X, 21D), and notifiable data breaches
-- (Part IIIC: ss 26WE, 26WF, 26WG, 26WH, 26WK, 26WL).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 104, compilation date 4 June 2026, includes amendments to Act No. 75, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00227), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03712.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0009 (subjects/au/requirements.jsonl), priority 1, raised 7 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave lives: chloe c043, c044; jake k048, k064, k075; daniel d044, d052. They ask: what a credit
-- reporting body may hold when a credit card is applied for at 21 (c043) and 24 (k048); whether Chloe can stop marketing calls
-- and texts (c044, APP 7); what may be listed when Jake's debts of $41,000 go to collectors (k064, defaults); what stays on
-- his credit file, and for how long, when his debt agreement completes on 31 May 2042 (k075, personal insolvency
-- information); whether Daniel's company Jarrah, under $3 million turnover with three employees in June 2031, is outside the
-- Act (d044, s 6D); and, in April 2036, above $3 million, whether a breach of 1,200 users' email addresses is an eligible data
-- breach, who must be told and by when (d052, Part IIIC). SCOPED to those questions and the definitions, conditions and
-- exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- Not encoded: the other twelve APPs; agencies, State authorities and registered political parties (s 6C(1) is read only
-- for the small business operator limb); s 6E (small business operators prescribed by regulation, AML/CTF reporting entities,
-- protected action ballot agents, registered employee associations, CDR accreditation); the employee records exemption (s
-- 7B(3)) and journalism exemption; the parts of Part IIIA about use and disclosure by credit reporting bodies (ss 20E-20N),
-- ban periods (s 20K), access and correction (ss 20R-20U), credit providers' use of credit eligibility information (ss 21G-
-- 21P), the CR code, repayment history beyond its retention period, and fraud (s 20Y); Part IIIC exceptions in ss 26WD,
-- 26WN, 26WP, 26WQ, the Commissioner's directions (s 26WR) and penalties. What a LENDER must assess before a credit card is
-- issued (c043, k048) is the National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009, not this Act. The National Personal Insolvency
-- Index (k075) is the Bankruptcy Act 1966.
--
-- DATES are written as numbers YYYYMMDD (2042-05-31 is 20420531), so that "the period of 5 years that starts on" a day D is
-- over on the day D + 50000 (its fifth anniversary) and later. A start on 29 February gives 29 February of a common year,
-- which still sorts between 28 February and 1 March. This is the encoder's convention, not the Act's.
--
-- AMOUNTS AS INPUTS. The $3,000,000 turnover test (s 6D) and the $150 default floor (s 6Q(1)(d)(i)) are stated in the Act.
-- The default floor may be raised by regulation ("such higher amount as is prescribed"), so the prescribed amount is an input.
-- The part-year turnover formula in s 6DA(2) is NOT in the deposit (the text ends "worked out using the formula:" and goes
-- straight to s 6E), so a part-year business's annual turnover is an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not available in this
-- session; the finished naive encodings in subjects/sg were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Privacy Act 1988 -- coverage, direct marketing, credit reporting, data breaches`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `ss 6C, 6D, 6DA, 6EA -- small business operators are not organisations`

-- s 6D(1): "A business is a small business at a time (the test time) in a financial year (the current year) if its annual
-- turnover for the previous financial year is $3,000,000 or less." (2): "if there was no time in the previous financial year
-- when the business was carried on, the business is a small business at the test time only if its annual turnover for the
-- current year is $3,000,000 or less."
-- s 6DA(1): annual turnover is the total "earned in the year in the course of the business" of sales proceeds, commission,
-- repair and service income, rent, leasing and hiring, government bounties and subsidies, interest, royalties and dividends,
-- and other operating income. (2): for part of a year, "the amount worked out using the formula:" -- the formula is missing
-- from the deposit. An INPUT here.
-- s 6D(3): a small business operator carries on one or more small businesses and "does not carry on a business that is not a
-- small business". (4): it is NOT one if it "(a) carries on a business that has had an annual turnover of more than
-- $3,000,000 for a financial year that has ended after the later of" starting the business and commencement; "(b) provides a
-- health service to another individual and holds any health information except in an employee record; or (c) discloses
-- personal information about another individual to anyone else for a benefit, service or advantage; or (d) provides a
-- benefit, service or advantage to collect personal information"; "(e) is a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth
-- contract"; "(f) is a credit reporting body". (7), (8): (c) and (d) are not engaged by disclosure or collection with consent
-- or as required or authorised by law. (9): a body corporate "related to a body corporate that carries on a business that is
-- not a small business" is not a small business operator.
-- s 6C(1): an organisation is an individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated association or trust "that is not a
-- small business operator", a registered political party, an agency or a State or Territory authority.
-- s 6EA(1): the Act applies to a small business operator "as if the operator were an organisation while a choice by the
-- operator to be treated as an organisation is registered".
-- Naive simplifications: one business per operator; (c) and (d) are one flag already narrowed by (7) and (8); the operator is
-- assumed not to be an agency, State authority or registered political party.
DECLARE Operator HAS
    `carried on the business at some time in the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `annual turnover for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
    `annual turnover for the current year` IS A NUMBER
    `highest annual turnover for any financial year ended since it started` IS A NUMBER
    `provides a health service and holds health information outside employee records` IS A BOOLEAN
    `trades in personal information without consent or legal authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a credit reporting body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a body corporate related to one with a business that is not small` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a registered choice to be treated as an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN

`the small business turnover limit` MEANS 3000000

GIVEN `the operator` IS AN Operator
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `its business is a small business` IF
    IF `the operator`'s `carried on the business at some time in the previous financial year`
    THEN `the operator`'s `annual turnover for the previous financial year` AT MOST `the small business turnover limit`
    ELSE `the operator`'s `annual turnover for the current year` AT MOST `the small business turnover limit`

GIVEN `the operator` IS AN Operator
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a small business operator` IF
        `its business is a small business` `the operator`
    AND (NOT `the operator`'s `highest annual turnover for any financial year ended since it started` GREATER THAN `the small business turnover limit`)
    AND (NOT `the operator`'s `provides a health service and holds health information outside employee records`)
    AND (NOT `the operator`'s `trades in personal information without consent or legal authority`)
    AND (NOT `the operator`'s `is a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract`)
    AND (NOT `the operator`'s `is a credit reporting body`)
    AND (NOT `the operator`'s `is a body corporate related to one with a business that is not small`)

GIVEN `the operator` IS AN Operator
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act binds it as an organisation` IF
        (NOT `it is a small business operator` `the operator`)
    OR  `the operator`'s `has a registered choice to be treated as an organisation`

§§ `Schedule 1, APP 7 -- direct marketing`

-- APP 7.1: "If an organisation holds personal information about an individual, the organisation must not use or disclose
-- the information for the purpose of direct marketing."
-- 7.2: it may, for information other than sensitive information, if "(a) the organisation collected the information from the
-- individual; and (b) the individual would reasonably expect" that use; "(c) the organisation provides a simple means by which
-- the individual may easily request not to receive direct marketing communications"; "(d) the individual has not made such a
-- request".
-- 7.3: it may, for information other than sensitive information, collected from the individual who would NOT reasonably
-- expect that use, or from someone else, if "(b) either: (i) the individual has consented ...; or (ii) it is impracticable to
-- obtain that consent", there is a simple opt-out, "(d) in each direct marketing communication" a prominent statement (or
-- other drawing of attention) that the individual may opt out, and "(e) the individual has not made such a request".
-- 7.4: sensitive information only "if the individual has consented". 7.5: contracted service providers meeting an obligation
-- under a Commonwealth contract.
-- 7.6, 7.7: the individual may request not to receive direct marketing communications; the organisation "must not charge"
-- and "must give effect to the request within a reasonable period".
-- 7.8: "This principle does not apply to the extent that any of the following apply: ... (a) the Do Not Call Register Act
-- 2006; (b) the Spam Act 2003".
-- Whether either of those Acts applies to a given call or message is a question for those Acts: an INPUT here.
DECLARE `Marketing use` HAS
    `the marketer is bound as an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Do Not Call Register Act or Spam Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is sensitive information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `collected from the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual would reasonably expect this use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent was impracticable to obtain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a simple opt-out means is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each communication states the individual may opt out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual has asked not to receive direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used by a contracted service provider to meet a Commonwealth contract obligation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A `Marketing use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `APP 7 governs the use` IF
        `the use`'s `the marketer is bound as an organisation`
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `the Do Not Call Register Act or Spam Act applies to it`)

GIVEN `the use` IS A `Marketing use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in APP 7.2 to 7.5 applies` IF
        (    (NOT `the use`'s `the information is sensitive information`)
         AND `the use`'s `collected from the individual`
         AND `the use`'s `the individual would reasonably expect this use`
         AND `the use`'s `a simple opt-out means is provided`
         AND (NOT `the use`'s `the individual has asked not to receive direct marketing`))
    OR  (    (NOT `the use`'s `the information is sensitive information`)
         AND ((NOT `the use`'s `collected from the individual`) OR (NOT `the use`'s `the individual would reasonably expect this use`))
         AND (`the use`'s `the individual consented` OR `the use`'s `consent was impracticable to obtain`)
         AND `the use`'s `a simple opt-out means is provided`
         AND `the use`'s `each communication states the individual may opt out`
         AND (NOT `the use`'s `the individual has asked not to receive direct marketing`))
    OR  (`the use`'s `the information is sensitive information` AND `the use`'s `the individual consented`)
    OR  `the use`'s `used by a contracted service provider to meet a Commonwealth contract obligation`

GIVEN `the use` IS A `Marketing use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `APP 7 forbids the use` IF
        `APP 7 governs the use` `the use`
    AND (NOT `an exception in APP 7.2 to 7.5 applies` `the use`)

-- APP 7.7(a): an opt-out request "must" be given effect "within a reasonable period", free of charge -- where APP 7 governs.
GIVEN `the use` IS A `Marketing use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `APP 7 obliges the marketer to honour an opt-out free of charge` IF
    `APP 7 governs the use` `the use`

§§ `ss 6N, 20C -- what a credit reporting body may hold`

-- s 6N: "Credit information about an individual is personal information (other than sensitive information) that is: (a)
-- identification information ...; (b) consumer credit liability information ...; (c) repayment history information ...; (ca)
-- financial hardship information ...; (d) a statement that an information request has been made ...; (e) the type of consumer
-- credit or commercial credit, and the amount of credit, sought in an application ...; (f) default information ...; (g)
-- payment information ...; (h) new arrangement information ...; (i) court proceedings information ...; (j) personal insolvency
-- information ...; (k) publicly available information" about activities in Australia and credit worthiness; "(l) the opinion
-- of a credit provider that the individual has committed ... a serious credit infringement".
-- Information about income, savings or employment is not in the list (the encoder's example of something that is not).
DECLARE `Kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `identification information`
    `consumer credit liability information`
    `repayment history information`
    `financial hardship information`
    `a statement that an information request was made`
    `the type and amount of credit sought in an application`
    `default information`
    `payment information`
    `new arrangement information`
    `court proceedings information`
    `personal insolvency information`
    `publicly available credit-worthiness information`
    `a serious credit infringement opinion`
    `sensitive information`
    `information about income or savings`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is credit information` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `sensitive information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `information about income or savings` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 20C(1): "A credit reporting body must not collect credit information about an individual." Civil penalty 2,000 penalty
-- units. (3): unless "(a) the credit reporting body collects the credit information ... from a credit provider who is
-- permitted under section 21D to disclose the information to the body; and (b) the body collects the information in the course
-- of carrying on a credit reporting business; and (c) if the information is identification information ... the body also
-- collects from the provider, or already holds, credit information of another kind". (2) required or authorised by law and
-- (4) collection from entities other than credit providers are not encoded.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information`, `the provider may disclose it under s 21D` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of a credit reporting business` IS A BOOLEAN, `the body has or collects another kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a credit reporting body may collect it from a credit provider` IF
        `it is credit information` `the kind`
    AND `the provider may disclose it under s 21D`
    AND `in the course of a credit reporting business`
    AND (CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `identification information` THEN `the body has or collects another kind`
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `ss 6Q, 21D -- default information and its listing`

-- s 6Q(1): default information is information about a payment the individual is overdue in making on consumer credit if
-- "(a) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making the payment; and (b) the provider has given a written notice to
-- the individual informing the individual of the overdue payment and requesting that the individual pay ...; and (c) the
-- provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from recovering the amount ...; and (d) the amount of the overdue
-- payment is equal to or more than: (i) $150; or (ii) such higher amount as is prescribed by the regulations."
-- s 21D(2), (3): a credit provider may disclose credit information to a credit reporting body only if it "(a)(i) is a member
-- of or subject to a recognised external dispute resolution scheme" (or prescribed), "(ii) knows, or believes on reasonable
-- grounds, that the individual is at least 18 years old", the body "(b) is ... an agency; or ... an organisation that has an
-- Australian link", and "(3)(a) the information does not relate to an act, omission, matter or thing that occurred or existed
-- before the individual turned 18"; "(b) ... the credit is or has been provided, or applied for, in Australia"; and for default
-- information "(d)(i) the credit provider has given the individual a notice in writing stating that the provider intends to
-- disclose the information ...; and (ii) at least 14 days have passed since the giving of the notice."
-- Naive simplifications: the repayment-history conditions in (3)(c) are not encoded; the ban period in s 21F is not encoded.
DECLARE `Overdue payment` HAS
    `days overdue` IS A NUMBER
    `written notice requesting payment given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recovery barred by a statute of limitations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount overdue` IS A NUMBER
    `higher amount prescribed by the regulations` IS A NUMBER

`the default floor in the Act` MEANS 150

GIVEN `the payment` IS AN `Overdue payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is default information` IF
        `the payment`'s `days overdue` AT LEAST 60
    AND `the payment`'s `written notice requesting payment given`
    AND (NOT `the payment`'s `recovery barred by a statute of limitations`)
    AND `the payment`'s `amount overdue` AT LEAST `the larger of` `the default floor in the Act` (`the payment`'s `higher amount prescribed by the regulations`)

DECLARE `Disclosure to a bureau` HAS
    `the kind disclosed` IS A `Kind of information`
    `the provider is in a recognised external dispute resolution scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider believes the individual is at least 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body is an agency or has an Australian link` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it relates to something before the individual turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit was provided or applied for in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of intention to disclose given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since that notice` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `Disclosure to a bureau`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21D permits the disclosure` IF
        `it is credit information` (`the disclosure`'s `the kind disclosed`)
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the provider is in a recognised external dispute resolution scheme`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the provider believes the individual is at least 18`
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the body is an agency or has an Australian link`
    AND (CONSIDER `the disclosure`'s `the kind disclosed`
         WHEN `identification information` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOT `the disclosure`'s `it relates to something before the individual turned 18`)
    AND `the disclosure`'s `the credit was provided or applied for in Australia`
    AND (CONSIDER `the disclosure`'s `the kind disclosed`
         WHEN `default information` THEN `the disclosure`'s `notice of intention to disclose given` AND `the disclosure`'s `days since that notice` AT LEAST 14
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `ss 20V, 20W -- retention periods`

-- s 20W table: consumer credit liability information, 2 years from termination; repayment history information, 2 years from
-- the due day; financial hardship information, 1 year from the due day; 6N(d) or (e) information, 5 years from the information
-- request; default information, "5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information";
-- payment information, 5 years from collection of the default information; new arrangement information (6S(1) and (2)), 2
-- years; court proceedings information, 5 years from the judgement; a serious credit infringement opinion (6N(l)), 7 years from
-- collection.
-- s 20V(1) note: "There is no retention period for identification information or credit information of a kind referred to in
-- paragraph 6N(k)." Personal insolvency information has its own section, 20X.
-- s 20V(2): the body "must destroy the credit information, or ensure that the information is de-identified, within 1 month
-- after the retention period for the information ends", civil penalty 1,000 penalty units; (3) not while a correction request
-- or dispute is pending; (4) not if a law or order requires retention.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20W fixes a retention period in years for it` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `identification information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `publicly available credit-worthiness information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `personal insolvency information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `sensitive information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `information about income or savings` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 20W retention period in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `consumer credit liability information` THEN 2
    WHEN `repayment history information` THEN 2
    WHEN `financial hardship information` THEN 1
    WHEN `a statement that an information request was made` THEN 5
    WHEN `the type and amount of credit sought in an application` THEN 5
    WHEN `default information` THEN 5
    WHEN `payment information` THEN 5
    WHEN `new arrangement information` THEN 2
    WHEN `court proceedings information` THEN 5
    WHEN `a serious credit infringement opinion` THEN 7
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information`, `the period starts on` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 20W retention period is over on` IF
        `s 20W fixes a retention period in years for it` `the kind`
    AND `the day` AT LEAST `the period starts on` PLUS 10000 TIMES `the s 20W retention period in years` `the kind`

§§ `s 20X -- personal insolvency information: debt agreements`

-- s 20X(1) table, retention period "whichever of the following periods ends later": item 4, "a debt agreement to which item 5
-- of this table does not apply": "(a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the
-- period of 2 years that starts on the day: (i) the agreement is terminated under the Bankruptcy Act; or (ii) an order
-- declaring that all the agreement is void is made". Item 5, "a debt agreement that ends under section 185N of the
-- Bankruptcy Act": "(a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period that ends
-- on the day on which the agreement ends."
-- So on completion under s 185N the information goes at the LATER of five years from the making and the day it ends.
-- Bankruptcies and personal insolvency agreements (items 1-3) and proposals (s 20X(2)) are not encoded.
DECLARE `How the agreement ended` IS ONE OF
    `ended under s 185N`
    `terminated or declared void`
    `not yet ended`

DECLARE `Debt agreement` HAS
    `made on` IS A NUMBER
    `how it ended` IS A `How the agreement ended`
    `ended on` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `Debt agreement`, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt agreement retention period is over on` IF
        `the day` AT LEAST `the agreement`'s `made on` PLUS 50000
    AND (CONSIDER `the agreement`'s `how it ended`
         WHEN `ended under s 185N` THEN `the day` GREATER THAN `the agreement`'s `ended on`
         WHEN `terminated or declared void` THEN `the day` AT LEAST `the agreement`'s `ended on` PLUS 20000
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `Part IIIC, ss 26WE, 26WF, 26WG -- eligible data breaches`

-- s 26WE(1)(a): the Part applies where "an APP entity holds personal information" and is bound by APP 11.1. (2): an eligible
-- data breach is "(a) ... unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information" where "(ii) a reasonable
-- person would conclude that the access or disclosure would be likely to result in serious harm to any of the individuals to
-- whom the information relates"; or "(b) the information is lost in circumstances where: (i) unauthorised access to, or
-- unauthorised disclosure of, the information is likely to occur" and serious harm would be likely if it did.
-- s 26WF(1), (3), (4): it "is not, and is taken never to have been" an eligible data breach if the entity's action, taken
-- before serious harm (or, for a loss, before any access), means a reasonable person would conclude serious harm is not
-- likely (or there is no access).
-- s 26WG: in deciding likely serious harm, have regard to the kind and sensitivity of the information, security measures and
-- the likelihood they could be overcome, who has or could obtain it, encryption and keys, the nature of the harm, and "any
-- other relevant matters". The Act gives no list of kinds that are or are not serious: an INPUT.
DECLARE `Kind of incident` IS ONE OF
    `unauthorised access or disclosure`
    `loss of the information`

DECLARE `Data incident` HAS
    `the entity is an APP entity bound by APP 11.1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what happened` IS A `Kind of incident`
    `after the loss, unauthorised access or disclosure is likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable person would conclude serious harm is likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `remedial action under s 26WF took it out` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Data incident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an eligible data breach` IF
        `the incident`'s `the entity is an APP entity bound by APP 11.1`
    AND `the incident`'s `a reasonable person would conclude serious harm is likely`
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `remedial action under s 26WF took it out`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the incident`'s `what happened`
         WHEN `unauthorised access or disclosure` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE `the incident`'s `after the loss, unauthorised access or disclosure is likely`)

§§ `Part IIIC, ss 26WH, 26WK, 26WL -- assessment and notification`

-- s 26WH(1), (2): where the entity "is aware that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that there may have been an eligible
-- data breach" but not that there are reasonable grounds to believe there has been one, it must "carry out a reasonable and
-- expeditious assessment" and "take all reasonable steps to ensure that the assessment is completed within 30 days after the
-- entity becomes aware".
-- s 26WK(2): where it is aware of reasonable grounds to believe there has been an eligible data breach it must prepare a
-- statement and "give a copy of the statement to the Commissioner", "as soon as practicable after the entity becomes so
-- aware". (3): identity and contact details, a description, the kinds of information, recommended steps for individuals.
-- s 26WL(2): it must "(a) if it is practicable ... notify the contents of the statement to each of the individuals to whom
-- the relevant information relates; or (b) if it is practicable ... to each of the individuals who are at risk", or "(c) if
-- neither paragraph (a) nor (b) applies: (i) publish a copy of the statement on the entity's website (if any); and (ii) take
-- reasonable steps to publicise" it. (3): "as soon as practicable after the completion of the preparation of the statement."
-- No section fixes a number of days for the statement or the notification. The 30 days is for the ASSESSMENT of a suspicion.
`the days within which reasonable steps must complete an assessment` MEANS 30

GIVEN `grounds to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN, `grounds to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an assessment under s 26WH is required` IF
    `grounds to suspect` AND (NOT `grounds to believe`)

GIVEN `the incident` IS A `Data incident`, `grounds to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statement must go to the Commissioner` IF
    `it is an eligible data breach` `the incident` AND `grounds to believe`

DECLARE `Notification route` IS ONE OF
    `notify every individual whose information it was, or only those at risk`
    `notify the individuals at risk`
    `publish the statement on its website and publicise it`

GIVEN `practicable to notify everyone` IS A BOOLEAN, `practicable to notify those at risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notification route`
`the notification route` MEANS
    IF `practicable to notify everyone`
    THEN `notify every individual whose information it was, or only those at risk`
    ELSE IF `practicable to notify those at risk`
         THEN `notify the individuals at risk`
         ELSE `publish the statement on its website and publicise it`
